---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import EmptyState from '../components/EmptyState.astro';
import ResultBadge from '../components/ResultBadge.astro';
import { EXPECTED, SITE_NAME } from '../config';
import { currentUpdates, hasPublication, latestCheckFor, publication, sites, totals } from '../lib/data';
import { date, num } from '../lib/format';
---
<Base title={SITE_NAME} kind="home">
  <section aria-labelledby="mission">
    <h1 id="mission">How persistently do Bay Area landfills leak methane, and did repairs change that?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This tracker reads back through public satellite and aircraft passes over five Bay Area landfills.
      It estimates how often each site was seen emitting and how much, tests whether a measured change
      followed each dated repair or inspection, and compares the satellite view with what operators report
      to the EPA. Regulators already learn about individual plumes; the gaps are persistence, follow-up and
      the comparison with reported figures.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="findings">
    <h2 id="findings">Latest findings</h2>
    {hasPublication ? (
      <>
        <div class="grid">
          <Card><span class="big">{num(totals.sites)}</span><span class="what">landfills watched</span></Card>
          <Card><span class="big">{num(totals.usablePasses)}</span><span class="what">usable passes, all instruments</span></Card>
          <Card><span class="big">{num(totals.plumeDays)}</span><span class="what">days with a plume seen</span></Card>
          <Card><span class="big">{num(totals.estimates)}</span><span class="what">sites with an estimate</span></Card>
        </div>
        <p class="muted">Counts follow how often a site was observed. A site that was flown more often shows more plumes; see plume days per usable pass on the <a href="/map/">map</a>.</p>
        <h3>Landfills</h3>
        <div class="grid">
          {sites.map((s) => {
            const latest = latestCheckFor(s.site_id ?? '');
            return (
              <Card title={s.name ?? s.site_id ?? ''} href={`/sites/${s.site_id}/`}>
                <p class="what">{s.city}, {s.county} County{s.status ? ` · ${s.status}` : ''}</p>
                <ResultBadge colour={latest?.colour} held={latest?.result_held} />
              </Card>
            );
          })}
        </div>
        <h3>Latest data update</h3>
        {currentUpdates.length ? (
          <ul>
            {currentUpdates.map((u) => (
              <li>{u.text} <span class="muted">({date(u.event_date)})</span></li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        ) : (
          <p class="muted">No change notes in this update.</p>
        )}
        <p>Data through {date(publication?.data_through)}. See <a href="/updates/">all updates</a>, the <a href="/checks/">past checks</a> and the <a href="/methods/">method checks</a>.</p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <EmptyState title="No results yet" expected={EXPECTED.publication}>
        <p>The pages are in place; counters, landfill cards and the latest update appear here once the first snapshot is published.</p>
      </EmptyState>
    )}
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="method">
    <h2 id="method">How it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>A satellite or aircraft passes over a landfill.</li>
      <li>It sees a plume, or it doesn't.</li>
      <li>Every pass counts, not just the ones with plumes.</li>
      <li>A statistical model gives each site a 90% range for how often it emits and how much.</li>
      <li>Control sites remove shifts that hit every site at once, such as a new instrument starting to fly.</li>
      <li>The results are compared with the figures operators report to the EPA.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>More in <a href="/methods/">Methods</a> and <a href="/how-to-read/">How to read this site</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="limits">
    <h2 id="limits">What satellites can't see</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Sentinel-2 only sees plumes of about 2 tonnes per hour or more, so it is a check on large events, not a main detector.</li>
      <li>Satellites only see in daytime and in clear skies.</li>
      <li>Annual figures are methane above a detection floor in those conditions, not a site's total emissions.</li>
      <li>Plumes close to another methane source are marked ambiguous and never assigned to a landfill.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="credits">
    <h2 id="credits">Data and credits</h2>
    <p>Built from public data: NASA EMIT, ESA Copernicus Sentinel-2, Carbon Mapper (non-commercial use), the US EPA Greenhouse Gas Reporting Program, Air District public records, CalRecycle and the US Census Bureau. Full credits and terms on the <a href="/data/">data page</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
